R"VG(
# news2.vg (H-04's second pass): the news's register, continued: the harvest, the land's disasters, the works opened, the ways, the
# inventions, the rule (a ruler's death, an accession, the government), a death of note, the unrest and the move to the cities.

news.harvest
  ($e.harvest=rich) {news.h.harv.r}\n{news.harv.r} {news.harv.t}
  ($e.harvest=failed|$e.harvest=poor) {news.h.harv.p}\n{news.harv.p} {news.harv.t}
news.h.harv.r
  Record harvest
  A good year
  Full barns
news.h.harv.p
  Poor harvest
  A thin year
  The harvest fails
news.harv.r
  The {crop} harvest is the largest in living memory; prices are expected to fall sharply.
  The barns of {$home} are full to the doors, and the {crop} is being stored in [the schoolrooms|the old market|the chapel|anywhere with a roof].
  The {crop} is so cheap at the markets {season.this} that the farmers are feeding it to the {herd}.
  From every district the same report: the {crop} heavy, the {fruit} early, and not enough hands to bring it all in.
news.harv.p
  The {crop} harvest has been poor across the land. Prices are rising.
  Rain at the wrong time and [frost|hail|the {pest}] at the worst have halved the {crop} in the upper valleys.
  The {crop} came in thin and late, and what came in is [mildewed|small|full of weeds].
  The {crop} has failed in the south and is poor in the north, and the {fruit} have not set at all.
news.harv.t
  The millers are said to be pleased, which is never a good sign for anyone else.
  {crop2} has done better than the {crop}, and the {fruit} better than both.
  There will be dancing at {$home} on the last day of the reaping, whatever the price, and {drink} after.
  The price of a loaf at {$home} is {n} {smallcoin}, and the bakers expect it to change.
  The farmers of {$home} meet at {town.open} on the rest day to agree a price for the {crop}, and to disagree about it.
  The {herd} will winter well, which is more than can be said for the farmers.

# ---- the land ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

news.flood
  {news.h.flood}\n{news.flood.m} {news.flood.x}
news.h.flood
  Floods at {$e.place}
  {$e.place} under water
  ($e.flood=river) The river rises
  ($e.flood=sea) The sea comes in
news.flood.m
  ($e.flood=river) The river has [burst its banks|come over the walls|risen over the lower town] at {$e.place}; {#$e.value:about} are reported drowned, and many more homeless.
  ($e.flood=sea) A great tide driven by the wind has broken the sea wall at {$e.place}; {#$e.value:about} are drowned, and the [harbour|fish market|boats] lost.
  The water stood {n} feet deep in the streets of {$e.place} for [three days|a week|eleven days], and {#$e.value:about} are dead.
  (has:$e.place.quarter) {$e.place.quarter} of {$e.place} is under water to the upper windows; the dead are put at {#$e.value:about}.
news.flood.x
  Boats are going from door to door with {food} and fresh water.
  The {herd} of the low farms were lost almost to the last.
  The {craft} works on the river will not open again {season.this}.
  {news.said} that the walls will be raised before the next {season.any}, as they were last time.
  The survivors are camped in {town.open} at {$e.place}, under sailcloth and {garment.n:pl}.
  (has:$e.place.landmark) Of {$e.place.landmark}, only the top can be seen.
  The {crop} in the low fields is under the water and will not come up again.

news.drought
  {news.h.drought}\n{news.drought.m} {news.drought.x}
news.h.drought
  Drought
  No rain
  The dry year
news.drought.m
  No rain has fallen for months. Water is being carted to the towns.
  The {watersrc.n} at {$home} is lower than anyone has seen it, and the {crop} is burning in the fields.
  ($e.value>1) This is the {#$e.value:ord} year of the drought, and the river can be walked across at {$home}.
  The {herd} are being sold for what they will fetch, because there is nothing to feed them on.
news.drought.x
  Water is to be sold by the bucket at {n} {smallcoin}, and never to the same house twice in a day.
  Prayers for rain at {holyplace} have been [well attended|answered by a dust storm|held every day this week].
  (inv.railway=1) The railway is carrying water in the {crop} wagons, and the {crop} is going nowhere.
  The council has forbidden the watering of gardens, which the gardens had already noticed.
  The {herd} are being driven to {mountain}, where there is said to be grass.
  The {fruit} are falling small and hard off the trees.

news.quake
  {news.h.quake}\n{news.quake.m} {news.quake.x}
news.h.quake
  Earthquake at {$e.place}
  The ground shakes
  {$e.place} in ruins
news.quake.m
  A severe earthquake struck {$e.place} [before dawn|at noon|in the night]; the dead are put at {#$e.value:about}.
  The ground shook at {$e.place} for [the time it takes to say a prayer|a long minute|longer than anyone can say], and when it stopped {#$e.value:about} were dead.
  (has:$e.place.landmark) {$e.place.landmark} came down in the earthquake at {$e.place}, with {#$e.value:about} dead in the streets round it.
news.quake.x
  The people of {$e.place} are sleeping in the open, afraid of their own roofs.
  Shocks were felt as far as {city}, where [the bells rang by themselves|crockery fell off the shelves|nobody slept].
  The {roofs} of the old town held better than the new ones, which will surprise nobody who has paid for a new one.
  Rescuers are digging with their hands in {town.open}.
  The {craft} works are standing but nobody will go in.
  (has:$e.place.landmark) {$e.place.landmark} still stands, and the people have gathered under it.

news.eruption
  {mountain} erupts\n{news.erupt.m} {news.erupt.x}
news.erupt.m
  Ash has fallen as far as {city}. The dead near {$e.place} are put at {#$e.value:about}.
  {mountain} has woken, and the fire came down its sides as far as {$e.place}, where {#$e.value:about} are dead.
news.erupt.x
  The sky over {$home} is brown at noon and the {bird} have gone quiet.
  The {crop} near the mountain is under a hand's depth of ash.
  The roads east are closed by the falls of stone, and the {herd} are being driven west.

news.impact
  ($e.impact=world) The sky goes dark\nThe object that struck the world has raised a cloud that covers the sky. {news.impact.x}
  ($e.impact!=world) Object falls near {$e.place}\nAn object from space has struck near {$e.place}, killing {#$e.value:about}. {news.impact.x}
  ($e.impact!=world) A stone from the sky\nA stone fell out of the sky {time.of} and struck the country near {$e.place}; {#$e.value:about} are dead and the {crop} for miles around is flattened. {news.impact.x}
news.impact.x
  Windows were broken as far as {city}.
  Nobody can say how long it will last, and the astronomers have stopped saying anything.
  Crowds went out to see the hole and the police turned them back.

news.flare
  The sun flares\nThe sun has flared; burns and blindness are reported across the day side, and {#$e.value:about} are dead. {news.flare.x}
news.flare.x
  Everyone is asked to stay under a roof at noon.
  (inv.telegraph=1) The telegraph lines burned through in a dozen places.
  The {herd} left in the fields are blind.

news.winter
  The cold continues\n{news.winter.m}
news.winter.m
  The winter shows no sign of ending. Coal is being rationed.
  The {watersrc.n} at {$home} has frozen solid and the river with it; the {herd} are being fed {crop} meant for bread.
  ($e.value>1) This is the {#$e.value:ord} winter without a summer between, and the old are saying they never saw the like.

# ---- the works and the ways ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

news.built
  {news.h.built}\n{news.built.m} {news.built.x}
news.h.built
  {$e.work} opened
  A new {$e.workkey} at {$e.place}
  Opening at {$e.place}
news.built.m
  {$e.work} at {$e.place}, {#$e.value|year} in the building, was opened yesterday with speeches.
  The new {$e.workkey} at {$e.place} was opened yesterday. It cost, the council admits, {news.cost}.
  (has:$e.a) {$e.a:full} cut the ribbon at the new {$e.workkey} of {$e.place} yesterday, {#$e.value|year} after the first stone.
  After {#$e.value|year} of scaffolding, {$e.work} at {$e.place} stands finished, in {walls.of} [and {colour.holy} paint|with {motif.over} over the doors|under {roofs}]. {=.desc}
news.built.x
  A band played {news.tune}, and the speeches were {news.speech}.
  The builders were given {drink} and the rest of the day.
  Visitors are admitted on the rest day, for {n} {smallcoin}.
  Some at {$e.place} say it is too big, and some say it is too late, and the {news.builders} say nothing.
  (has:gazette) An engraving of it, with {news.engr}, will appear next week in {gazette}.
  (!has:.desc) It is built of {walls.of}, with {motif.over} cut over the doors.
news.tune
  the {festival} march
  on {instrument}
  until it rained
  something nobody recognised
news.speech
  long
  longer than the building took
  in the old style
  mercifully short

news.way
  ($e.out=2) New line opened\n{news.way.rail} {news.way.x}
  ($e.out=3) The canal\nThe canal between {$e.place} and {$e.place2} was opened yesterday; the first barge carried {crop} and a band. {news.way.x}
  ($e.out!=2 $e.out!=3) {news.h.way}\nThe road between {$e.place} and {$e.place2} was opened yesterday[; the carters are pleased|, a year late|, with speeches]. {news.way.x}
news.h.way
  A new road
  The way is open
  {$e.place} to {$e.place2}
news.way.rail
  The railway between {$e.place} and {$e.place2} was opened yesterday; the journey now takes [a day|half a day|an afternoon].
  The first train ran from {$e.place} to {$e.place2} yesterday with the council aboard and {herd} on the line, which delayed it.
news.way.x
  The tolls will be {n} {smallcoin} a cart and nothing for a walker.
  The inns along the old road are said to be worried.
  The {crop} of the valley will be at the markets of {city} in half the time.
  Children lined the way to watch, and some of them are still there.
  The first to use it was a farmer with {n} {herd}, who did not know it was opening.

news.invention
  {news.h.inv}\n{news.inv.m} {news.inv.t}
news.h.inv
  A new invention
  {$e.invention}
  A marvel at {$e.place}
news.inv.m
  (has:$e.a) {$e.a:name} of {$e.place} has demonstrated {$e.invention} before an audience of the learned.
  (has:$e.a) A demonstration of {$e.invention} at {$e.place} drew crowds yesterday; its maker, {$e.a:name}, answered questions for an hour.
  {$e.invention} was shown at {$e.place} yesterday, and the hall was full an hour before the doors opened.
news.inv.t
  Investors from {news.inv.where} are said to be interested.
  Some in the audience left before the end, holding their {garment.n:pl} over their heads.
  The inventor declined to say what it would cost, and would say only that it would not need {fuel}.
  The guild of the {craft} trade has asked what it will do to them, and has not been answered.
  (has:$e.a) {$e.a:name} is a {$e.a.trade} by trade, and says the idea came at the {news.time.of.x}.
news.inv.where
  {city}
  the coast
  the {craft} guild
  over the sea
news.time.of.x
  noon meal
  first light
  end of a long day
  wrong moment
news.builders
  builders
  masons
  {craft} masters
  carters who carried the stone
news.cost
  twice what was promised
  {n} {coin} more than was voted
  a third more than the {craft} guild paid for its hall
  more than the {festival} fair brings in a year
news.engr
  the builders in front
  the council in front of the builders
  a {beast} that would not move out of the way
  the {colour.holy} flags flying
)VG"
